{"name":"Breezy","hex":"#c2dde6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"breezy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["With a breeze blowing, with a lively wind, pleasantly windy.","With a cheerful, casual, lively and light-hearted manner."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breezy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breezy","blocks":[{"text":"Breezy is a 1973 American romantic drama film directed by Clint Eastwood, produced by Robert Daley, and written by Jo Heims. The film stars William Holden and Kay Lenz, with Roger C. Carmel, Marj Dusay, and Joan Hotchkis in supporting roles. It is the third film directed by Eastwood and the first without him starring in it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Breezyfilmposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breezy","wikidata":"Q653251"},{"title":"Breezy (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Breezy is the tenth studio album by the American singer Chris Brown, released on June 24, 2022, as the follow-up to his 2019 album Indigo. The artists featured on the album are Lil Wayne, Anderson .Paak, Blxst, Lil Baby, H.E.R., EST Gee, Wizkid, Jack Harlow, Tory Lanez, Fivio Foreign, Ella Mai, Yung Bleu, Capella Grey, Lil Durk, Davido, and Bryson Tiller."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Chris_Brown_-_Breezy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breezy_(album)","wikidata":"Q110275890"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/The_Breezy_sign.jpg/500px-The_Breezy_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/The_Breezy_sign.jpg/500px-The_Breezy_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail"